        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": ">>    (I have also tried nvim-nightly but found it far too unstable to use regularly.)\n>\n> elaborate? 0.13 has significant changes to LSP/diagnostics. can't spend time on issues that may already be resolved.\n\nI've also seen errors when jumping to files on nightly -- I originally switched to nightly in hopes of solving these issues. But additionally, nightly introduced issues with my workflow (dir.vim breaking dirvish, lua api changes temporarily broke neovide gui, probably others that were fixed after updating). These are the kinds of breakages I'd expect from nightly, which is why I switched back to the stable version.\n\nWould you accept a patch to 0.12 to silence these errors but is never merged to master? I didn't see these issues on 0.11, so it'd be great if they were resolved in the stable branch.",
